+20 Nov 2026
+PHP Conference Kansai 2026 (JAPAN)
+We are excited to announce PHP Conference Kansai 2026! 🎉
+About the conference
+PHP Conference Kansai is a technical conference where PHP engineers in the Kansai region of Japan share their knowledge and experience.
+It started in 2011 and came back in 2024 in Osaka after a six-year break.
+It was held in Kobe in 2025, and this edition will be held in Kyoto.
+The theme of this edition is "次は、ここから始まる。" (What's next starts here.)
+AI has dramatically changed the way we work.
+But the quality of the answers you get from AI depends on how much you know when you ask.
+To ask the right questions and judge whether an answer holds up, you need to learn from others and see beyond your own perspective.
+At the conference, through sessions, talks, and casual conversations around the venue, you can talk with people who have a shared knowledge base.
+We want it to be a place where everyone who comes finds their own "next."
+Note: Despite its name, the conference takes place in January 2027.
+Who can join?
+Anyone involved with PHP is welcome, whether you use it now, used it before, or are just curious about it.
+(All talks will be in Japanese.)
+Basic facts
+Date: January 16, 2027 (JST)
+Location: Kyoto Research Park, Building 4, Kyoto, Japan
+Timetable
+Tickets
